WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.639 --> 00:00:06.569
As the X-Men square off against Apocalypse
and his four horsemen, there's no shortage

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:10.930
of spoilerific secrets in the latest mutant
slugfest. If there's anything to learn from

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:15.529
Apocalypse taking on Professor X's band of
heroes, it's that the 1980s and the ancient

00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:19.699
evil villain are both pretty much immortal.
Put on your neon-colored parachute pants.

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:23.650
We've made you an X-Men: Apocalypse Easter
egg omelette so dense you'd need adamantium

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.609
claws to cut through it. And just in case
you missed it, here’s your final warning:

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:29.720
there are major spoilers ahead!

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.869
Jabs at The Last Stand

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:34.590
One of X-Men: Apocalypse's most meta Easter
eggs comes while some young mutants pull a

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.480
Ferris Bueller and ditch a school day, hitting
up the mall instead. Surprisingly, the Dazzler

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.940
record scene we've seen in pictures prior
to the film's release was nowhere to be found

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.090
in the actual film. Instead, the group takes
a few jabs at the more underwhelming parts

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:51.769
of the X-Men film franchise. As the four mutant
teens leave a showing of Return of the Jedi,

00:00:51.769 --> 00:00:55.739
they joke about how sequels always end up
being much darker than the first film. Even

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:59.559
though they’re talking about Star Wars,
it’s also a pretty clear reference to X2:

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:04.360
X-Men United. Jean Grey adds that everyone
knows that the third movie is almost always

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.900
the weakest of the bunch, which is almost
definitely a zinger aimed at X-Men: The Last

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.299
Stand — the third movie in the franchise that
most fans pretend never happened. In case

00:01:13.299 --> 00:01:17.049
you were wondering, frequent X-Men director
Bryan Singer skipped out on filming The Last

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:20.430
Stand in favor of Superman Returns.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.920
Return of The Blob

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.280
In a callback to Wolverine's debut in the
original X-Men film and X-Men Origins: Wolverine,

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.899
we’re treated to some mutant-filled, underground
fights. Before we see Angel taking on Nightcrawler,

00:01:30.899 --> 00:01:35.719
we see a familiar face laid out on the ground
from a previous fight. This is Fred Dukes,

00:01:35.719 --> 00:01:40.250
better known as The Blob. Dukes being flat
on his back is probably a callback to his

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:45.020
appearance in Origins. This time, he looks
even more comic-accurate. Good luck to the

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.479
guys who had to carry him out of the ring.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:50.280
Star Trek appreciation

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.700
Bryan Singer isn't ashamed of being a Trekkie.
When we visit Storm's home, her television

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:59.329
is playing the original Star Trek series'
season two episode, "Who Mourns for Adonais."

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:03.789
This Trek episode foreshadows future events
with Apocalypse, as it focuses on the team

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:09.200
encountering a powerful god-like character
who can grow to amazing heights. Sound familiar? Singer also

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.450
appeared as an uncredited crew member in Star
Trek: Nemesis, taking orders from the original

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.890
Professor X himself, Patrick Stewart.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.340
Stan Lee's cameo co-star

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:23.420
We've seen Stan Lee cameo as a postman, Hugh
Hefner, Larry King, an intergalactic ladies'

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:31.340
man, and even a strip club DJ. In X-Men: Apocalypse,
Lee's role is much simpler. We see him react

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.980
to something horrific. The big difference
from his previous cameos is who's with him

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.890
this time around. With Lee during this scene
is his real-life wife, Joan.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.319
Reloading Weapon X

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:45.409
The last X-Men: Apocalypse trailer teased
Hugh Jackman's return for the we've-lost-counteenth

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:50.330
time as Wolverine. The film gives Logan his
adamantium skeleton from the Weapon X program,

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.900
rewriting Origins' story even further, along
with his trademark, trauma-induced berserker

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.480
rage. Best of all, Jackman actually &nbsp;wears
the iconic Weapon X headgear, straight from

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.560
the comics. Don't hold your breath for the
character's famous yellow spandex costume though.

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:06.580
Another Order of the Phoenix

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:11.129
Speaking of Wolverine, the character's longtime
love interest Jean Grey is only in her teens

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:15.299
during the film, and she's still struggling
to control her powers. Jean Grey has nightmares

00:03:15.299 --> 00:03:19.780
about what's going to happen, teasing the
inevitable fight against Apocalypse's forces.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.110
She also alludes to seeing flames and a darkness
inside her, foreshadowing her character's

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.709
eventual possession by the cosmic entity known
as the Phoenix.

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:31.549
In both X-Men: The Last Stand and the original
comic books, Jean struggles with controlling

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:36.030
the fiery Phoenix before it takes over completely,
turning her into one of the series' most powerful

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:40.189
villains. Towards the end of X-Men: Apocalypse,
Jean throws her worries out the window after

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:45.349
Xavier tells her to go all out on Apocalypse.
Jean turns her powers on full blast, resulting

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:49.349
in a flaming bird aura appearing around her,
teasing the Phoenix for a future entry of

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:53.980
the series. Yes, we got chills from it, and
so will you. Hopefully if they revisit the

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:58.319
Phoenix saga in future movies, it'll go a
little better this time around.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:02.159
That Sinister post-credits scene
As usual the movie's post-credits scene will

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:06.319
leave comic junkies jumping for joy, while
the average moviegoer will just have to wait

00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:10.560
until a comic fan explains it to them. The
final scene features a man in a suit exploring

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.099
the ruins of William Stryker's Weapon X compound.
As a cleanup crew tries mopping up the mess

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:19.690
of bullets and bodies, the man grabs some
Weapon X samples and stows them in his briefcase.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:23.420
The briefcase snaps shut, showing a logo of
a company named "Essex Corp."

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.300
Comics fans know that Nathaniel Essex, also
known as Mr. Sinister, is a longtime villain

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:33.000
of the X-Men. He frequently collaborates with
Apocalypse, and he's obsessed with Jean Grey

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.430
and Scott Summers' genetics. He goes as far
as creating a clone of Jean Grey, Madelyne

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:42.270
Pryor, who Scott Summers marries and has a
kid with. That child turns out to be Cable,

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:47.030
Deadpool's time-traveling buddy. This could
set up Mr. Sinister in a future X-Men film

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:51.740
and maybe even the fan favorite character
of X-23, a young female clone of Wolverine.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:55.850
If 20th Century Fox is looking for a way to
make more Wolverine movies after Hugh Jackman

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.650
hangs up his claws, bringing X-23 into the
fold may just do the trick...

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:03.510
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.390
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which Easter Egg from X-Men: Apocalypse

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.100
was your favorite...

